  "ingredients": [
    "2 tablespoons olive oil",
    "1 small onion, finely chopped",
    "1 leek, chopped",
    "1 clove garlic, minced",
    "2 pounds ground beef",
    "2 teaspoons ground cumin",
    "2 teaspoons ground cardamom",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "1 teaspoon pepper",
    "1 tablespoon all-purpose flour",
    "1 tablespoon water, or as needed",
    "1 (14 ounce) package spring roll wrappers",
    "1 quart oil for frying, or as needed"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ddXRDtxotTnG8tIFJaDYITIsLFk=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-53603-sambusa-VAT-step-01-422670a0e1074d4eaf4f4ebf11ba30ee.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/53603/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium-low heat. Add onion, leek, and garlic; cook and stir until onion is transparent. Add ground beef; cook and stir until still slightly pink and about halfway done.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/_9Iy1fVaWJXNAlobTC1PFXaZ7Pw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-53603-sambusa-VAT-step-02-1-ab4d81ac3c654d23abf7913235fef6b7.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/53603/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Season with cumin, cardamom, salt, and pepper; mix well. Continue cooking until beef is browned and crumbly. Remove the skillet from heat.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/zrTzqnXEvY3OXhObSiLCzSWKx1w=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-53603-sambusa-VAT-step-03-1-18d36878185541fc93a4bc9af4ccb199.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/53603/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix flour and water together in a small bowl to make a thin paste. Using one wrapper at a time, fold into the shape of a cone.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/3BH6Y_QVpp8a3QPKdvIZ9VBhqhQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-53603-sambusa-VAT-step-04-87256994245046f0b73a48217d49446d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/53603/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fill cone with beef mixture, close the top, and seal with paste. Repeat until wrappers or filling are used up.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/bDoh4QFzspXJG5JW6-P3M5Je-00=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-53603-sambusa-VAT-step-05-e15117a4d3a6462b8fb47a423f3ff770.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/53603/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat oil in a deep fryer or large saucepan to 365 degrees F (170 degrees C). There should be enough oil to submerge sambusas. Fry sambusas, a few at a time, in hot oil until golden brown.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/nK5wB4iH5XaCAWjPC__U_x3fecQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-53603-sambusa-VAT-step-06-2933987dac7e42b3ae4c6e7ea4c97276.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/53603/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove to a paper towel-lined plate to drain.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/N5JDdb6J-HB0sm70-1ZejTPABOs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-53603-sambusa-VAT-step-07-469807f708264a7892b704debbc30a98.jpg"
